; A third module, so `Shadowed.ax` can make a call that its own module
; does NOT define and that the entry file does not define either - the
; term in `850-module-local-binding.ax` that fails if the module-local
; rule REPLACED the existing lookup rather than preceding it.
;
; It is a separate module rather than an undefined name so that
; `Shadowed.ax` resolves standalone: the diagnostics sweep checks every
; file of this tree on its own, and a module that references a name
; nothing it imports defines is an honest `AX3001` there.
(pub :: bump (-> Int Int))

(pub fn (bump x) (+ x 100))
